<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Porrentruy</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Porrentruy is a town in the canton of Jura in north-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/switzerland">Switzerland</a>, near the French border. After the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/protestant-reformation">Reformation</a> reached Basel, the prince-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">bishops</a> of Basel made its castle their residence until the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/french-revolution">French Revolution</a>. In 1792 the short-lived Rauracian Republic was proclaimed there.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/porrentruy.jpg" alt="Porrentruy" width="320" height="472" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Porrentruy_Altstadt.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
